#!markdown

# 03 · Portfolio Optimization

**English.** Modern portfolio theory chooses weights by trading expected return against risk. `Finance.Portfolio` covers the PyPortfolioOpt toolbox: return and risk estimators, mean-variance optimisation (minimum volatility, maximum Sharpe, efficient frontier), Black-Litterman, risk parity, Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP), CVaR optimisation and discrete allocation into whole shares.

**Bahasa Indonesia.** Teori portofolio modern memilih bobot dengan menimbang imbal hasil yang diharapkan terhadap risiko. `Finance.Portfolio` mencakup perangkat PyPortfolioOpt: estimator imbal hasil dan risiko, optimisasi mean-variance (volatilitas minimum, Sharpe maksimum, efficient frontier), Black-Litterman, risk parity, Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP), optimisasi CVaR, dan alokasi diskret ke jumlah saham bulat.

> Dibuat oleh Gravicode Studios dipimpin oleh Kang Fadhil

#!csharp

#i "nuget: ../artifacts/packages"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.Core, 0.6.0"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.Math, 0.6.0"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.Portfolio, 0.6.0"
#r "nuget: Gravicode.Finance.Visualization, 0.6.0"

using Finance.Core.Market;
using Finance.Mathematics;
using Finance.Portfolio;
using Finance.Visualization;

#!markdown

## Data and estimators / Data dan estimator

**EN.** Six synthetic assets with a realistic correlation structure (equities move together, bonds and gold diversify). Expected returns are annualised historical means; the covariance matrix uses Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage, which is far more stable than the raw sample covariance when history is short.

**ID.** Enam aset sintetis dengan struktur korelasi yang realistis (saham bergerak bersama, obligasi dan emas memberi diversifikasi). Imbal hasil yang diharapkan adalah rata-rata historis tahunan; matriks kovarians memakai shrinkage Ledoit-Wolf yang jauh lebih stabil daripada kovarians sampel ketika data historis pendek.

#!csharp

string[] assets = { "US Equity", "Tech", "EM Equity", "Bonds", "Gold", "REITs" };
double[] drift = { 0.08, 0.13, 0.10, 0.035, 0.05, 0.07 };
double[] vol = { 0.16, 0.28, 0.24, 0.06, 0.15, 0.20 };
double[,] corr =
{
    { 1.00, 0.80, 0.70, -0.20, 0.05, 0.60 },
    { 0.80, 1.00, 0.65, -0.25, 0.00, 0.50 },
    { 0.70, 0.65, 1.00, -0.10, 0.15, 0.55 },
    { -0.20, -0.25, -0.10, 1.00, 0.30, 0.10 },
    { 0.05, 0.00, 0.15, 0.30, 1.00, 0.10 },
    { 0.60, 0.50, 0.55, 0.10, 0.10, 1.00 },
};
var prices = Matrix.FromRows(SyntheticMarket.CorrelatedPrices(1260, drift, vol, corr, seed: 2024));
var returns = ExpectedReturns.ReturnsFromPrices(prices);
var mu = ExpectedReturns.MeanHistorical(returns);
var sigma = RiskModels.LedoitWolf(returns);
for (int i = 0; i < assets.Length; i++)
    Console.WriteLine($"{assets[i],-10} expected {mu[i],7:P2}  vol {Math.Sqrt(sigma[i, i]),7:P2}");
display(HTML(Charts.Heatmap(Stats.CovarianceToCorrelation(sigma), assets, new ChartOptions { Title = "Correlation (Ledoit-Wolf)", Height = 420, Width = 620 })));

#!markdown

## Mean-variance / Mean-variance

**EN.** The minimum-volatility portfolio ignores expected returns; the maximum-Sharpe (tangency) portfolio maximises return per unit of risk. Bounds here are long-only with a 40% cap per asset.

**ID.** Portofolio volatilitas minimum mengabaikan imbal hasil yang diharapkan; portofolio Sharpe maksimum (tangency) memaksimalkan imbal hasil per unit risiko. Batasan di sini hanya posisi beli (long-only) dengan batas 40% per aset.

#!csharp

var mvo = new MeanVarianceOptimizer(mu, sigma, lowerBound: 0, upperBound: 0.40, assets: assets);
var minVol = mvo.MinVolatility();
var maxSharpe = mvo.MaxSharpe(riskFreeRate: 0.02);
Console.WriteLine("Min volatility: " + minVol.Clean());
Console.WriteLine("  " + mvo.Performance(minVol, 0.02));
Console.WriteLine("Max Sharpe:     " + maxSharpe.Clean());
Console.WriteLine("  " + mvo.Performance(maxSharpe, 0.02));

var frontier = mvo.EfficientFrontier(40, 0.02);
var curve = new ScatterSeries("Efficient frontier", frontier.Select(p => p.Volatility).ToArray(), frontier.Select(p => p.ExpectedReturn).ToArray()) { Connect = true, Color = "#FBBF24" };
var singles = new ScatterSeries("Assets", assets.Select((_, i) => Math.Sqrt(sigma[i, i])).ToArray(), mu) { Labels = assets, Color = "#38BDF8" };
var pMin = mvo.Performance(minVol, 0.02);
var pMax = mvo.Performance(maxSharpe, 0.02);
display(HTML(Charts.Scatter(new[] { curve, singles },
    new ChartOptions { Title = "Efficient frontier", XLabel = "Volatility", YLabel = "Expected return", XFormat = "P0", YFormat = "P0", Height = 440 },
    new[] { new ChartMarker(pMin.Volatility, pMin.ExpectedReturn, "Min vol"), new ChartMarker(pMax.Volatility, pMax.ExpectedReturn, "Max Sharpe", "#2DD4BF") })));

#!markdown

## Black-Litterman

**EN.** Black-Litterman starts from the returns implied by market capitalisations (what the market "believes"), then blends in investor views weighted by confidence. Here: Tech outperforms US Equity by 3%, and Gold returns 7%.

**ID.** Black-Litterman berangkat dari imbal hasil yang tersirat dari kapitalisasi pasar (apa yang "diyakini" pasar), lalu memadukan pandangan investor yang ditimbang berdasarkan tingkat keyakinan. Di sini: Tech mengungguli US Equity sebesar 3%, dan Gold menghasilkan 7%.

#!csharp

double[] caps = { 45, 20, 10, 15, 5, 5 };
var prior = BlackLittermanModel.MarketImpliedPriorReturns(caps, sigma, riskAversion: 2.5, riskFreeRate: 0.02);
var views = new BlackLittermanViews(assets)
    .Relative("Tech", "US Equity", 0.03, confidence: 0.6)
    .Absolute("Gold", 0.07, confidence: 0.4);
var bl = BlackLittermanModel.Create(sigma, prior, views);
for (int i = 0; i < assets.Length; i++)
    Console.WriteLine($"{assets[i],-10} prior {prior[i],7:P2} → posterior {bl.Posterior[i],7:P2}");
Console.WriteLine("BL weights: " + bl.Weights(2.5).Clean());

#!markdown

## Risk-based portfolios / Portofolio berbasis risiko

**EN.** Risk parity equalises each asset's contribution to total volatility. HRP (López de Prado) clusters assets by correlation and splits risk down the dendrogram, avoiding the matrix inversion that makes mean-variance fragile.

**ID.** Risk parity menyamakan kontribusi setiap aset terhadap volatilitas total. HRP (López de Prado) mengelompokkan aset berdasarkan korelasi lalu membagi risiko menyusuri dendrogram, sehingga menghindari inversi matriks yang membuat mean-variance rapuh.

#!csharp

var erc = RiskParity.EqualRiskContribution(sigma, assets);
var rc = RiskParity.RiskContributions(erc.ToArray(), sigma);
Console.WriteLine("Risk parity:  " + erc.Clean());
Console.WriteLine("  risk contributions: " + string.Join(", ", rc.Select(x => (x / rc.Sum()).ToString("P1"))));

var hrp = HierarchicalRiskParity.Optimize(sigma, assets);
Console.WriteLine("HRP:          " + hrp.Weights.Clean());
Console.WriteLine("  cluster order: " + string.Join(" | ", hrp.Order.Select(i => assets[i])));

var inverseVol = HeuristicPortfolios.InverseVolatility(sigma, assets);
var maxDiv = HeuristicPortfolios.MaxDiversification(sigma, assets: assets);
Console.WriteLine($"Inverse vol diversification ratio {HeuristicPortfolios.DiversificationRatio(inverseVol.ToArray(), sigma):F3}; max-diversification {HeuristicPortfolios.DiversificationRatio(maxDiv.ToArray(), sigma):F3}");

display(HTML(Charts.Bar(assets, hrp.Weights.ToArray(), new ChartOptions { Title = "HRP weights", YFormat = "P0", Height = 300 })));

#!markdown

## CVaR optimisation / Optimisasi CVaR

**EN.** Variance treats upside and downside alike. CVaR optimisation (Rockafellar-Uryasev) minimises the average loss in the worst 5% of scenarios, using the historical returns directly as scenarios.

**ID.** Varians memperlakukan kenaikan dan penurunan secara sama. Optimisasi CVaR (Rockafellar-Uryasev) meminimalkan rata-rata kerugian pada 5% skenario terburuk, dengan memakai imbal hasil historis langsung sebagai skenario.

#!csharp

var cvarOpt = new CVaROptimizer(returns, beta: 0.95, upperBound: 0.40, assets: assets);
var minCvar = cvarOpt.MinCVaR();
Console.WriteLine("Min CVaR:     " + minCvar.Clean());
Console.WriteLine($"  daily CVaR95 {cvarOpt.CVaR(minCvar.ToArray()):P3} vs max-Sharpe {cvarOpt.CVaR(maxSharpe.ToArray()):P3}");

#!markdown

## Discrete allocation / Alokasi diskret

**EN.** Weights must become whole shares. The largest-remainder method gets as close as possible to the target weights for a given budget.

**ID.** Bobot harus diubah menjadi jumlah saham bulat. Metode largest-remainder mendekati bobot target sedekat mungkin untuk anggaran tertentu.

#!csharp

double[] lastPrices = Enumerable.Range(0, assets.Length).Select(i => prices[prices.Rows - 1, i]).ToArray();
var alloc = DiscreteAllocation.LargestRemainder(maxSharpe, lastPrices, budget: 50_000);
foreach (var (asset, shares) in alloc.Shares.Where(s => s.Value > 0))
    Console.WriteLine($"{asset,-10} {shares,5} shares");
Console.WriteLine($"Leftover cash: {alloc.Leftover:C2}");
